{"step_index":147,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:49:57Z","thinking":"**Assembling the proof.**\n\nThe inequalities `a ≤ k`, `k ≤ n`, and `k ≤ a` all worked definitionally. Also, several `Option.getD` equations are definitional. Now attempting to assemble the entire proof in `scratch.lean`.\n\n\n**Proving cardinality inequality.**\n\nDefined a function `f` mapping vertices to edges within an edge cover, using the axiom of choice. This function maps independent set vertices to the edge cover set. Showing that `f` maps an independent set `I` to the edge cover `s`.\n\nProving that `f` is injective on the independent set, assuming contradiction and constructing an edge that's in the edge set but also contradicts the independence of the set. This shows the injection.\n\n\n**Establishing cardinality relation.**\n\nProving `Finset.card_le_card_of_injOn f hmaps hinj` by constructing an injection.  Considering the maximum independent set `alpha` and the minimum edge cover size `rho`. The goal is to show `alpha ≤ rho`.\n\nThe cases for the minimum edge cover being `top` or some `rho` are addressed, the proof handles the trivial case `alpha ≤ Fintype.card V` when the minimum doesn't exist. Now handling the general case, where there exists some minimum rho.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > scratch.lean\\nimport Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nset_option maxRecDepth 10000\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph Finset\\n\\nabbrev Candidate : Prop :=\\n    ∀ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj],\\n      GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G → GraphCalc.HasEdgeCover G → GraphCalc.indepNum G ≤ GraphCalc.edgeCoverNumber G\\n\\nlemma sym2_eq_of_ne_mem {V : Type*} [DecidableEq V] (u v : V) (e : Sym2 V)\\n    (hu : u ∈ e) (hv : v ∈ e) (hne : u ≠ v) : e = s(u, v) := by\\n  induction e using Sym2.inductionOn with\\n  | hf a b =>\\n   