{"step_index":166,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:50:46Z","thinking":"**Constructing proof structure**\n\nThe code defines a function that appears to generate elements for a formal proof.  It normalizes input and determines the direction (prove or refute). Based on the direction, a corresponding header and pristine (initial) proof structure are generated.  The core structure establishes the theorem statement and its initial 'by' clause for subsequent proof steps.\n\n\n**Analyzing proof verification structure**\n\nThe code generates verification theorems by analyzing the generated proof attempt. It strips parts of the original attempt and confirms its structure. The function ensures the proof's target type matches the expected type, constructing a verification theorem from the original proof's result. This verification theorem essentially asserts that the original theorem is indeed of the claimed type.\n\n\n**Verifying generated file structure**\n\nThe task involves generating a specific Lean file structure. It necessitates preserving code up to a definition, followed by helper lemmas, and then prove/refute theorems. The script checks for the correct structure, verifying the presence of the `Candidate` definition, lemmas and the theorem statements. This validation includes the format and the correctness of the generated `lean` file.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > Challenge_1facfd37.lean\\nimport Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nset_option maxRecDepth 10000\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\\n-- Conjecture under test: (nontrivial) ⇒ independence_number ≤ edge_cover_number\\n-- Both declarations refer to the same `Candidate`.\\nabbrev Candidate : Prop :=\\n    ∀ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj],\\n      GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G → GraphCalc.HasEdgeCover G → GraphCalc.indepNum G ≤ GraphCalc.edgeCoverNumber G\\n\\nlemma sym2_eq_of_ne_mem {V : Type*} [DecidableEq V] (u v : V) (e : Sym2 V)\\n    (hu : u ∈ e) (hv : v ∈ e) (hne : u ≠ v) : e = s(u, v) := by\\n  induction e using Sym2.inductionOn with\\n  | hf a b =>\\n    rw [Sym2.mem_iff] at hu hv\\n    rcases hu with rfl | rfl <;> rcases hv with rfl | rfl\\n    · contradiction\\n    · rfl\\n    · exact Sym2.eq_swap\\n    · contradiction\\n\\nlemma indep_card_le_edge_cover_card {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    (I : Finset V) (hI : GraphCalc.IsIndependentFinset G I)\\n    (s : Finset (Sym2 V)) (hs_sub : s ⊆ G.edgeFinset) (hs_cov : GraphCalc.IsEdgeCoverFinset G s) :\\n    I.card ≤ s.card := by\\n  let f : V → Sym2 V := fun v => Classical.choose (hs_cov v)\\n  have hf_spec : ∀ v, f v ∈ s ∧ v ∈ f v := fun v => Classical.choose_spec (hs_cov v)\\n  have hmaps : Set.MapsTo f (↑I) (↑s) := by\\n    intro v _\\n    exact (hf_spec v).1\\n  have hinj : Set.InjOn f (↑I) := by\\n    intro u hu v hv heq\\n    by_contra hne\\n    have hu_e : u ∈ f u := (hf_spec u).2\\n    have hv_e : v ∈ f u := by rw [heq]; exact (hf_spec v).2\\n    have he_eq : f u = s(u, v) := sym2_eq_of_ne_mem u v (f u) hu_e hv_e hne\\n    have he_in_s : f u ∈ s := (hf_spec u).1\\n    have he_in_edges : f u ∈ G.edgeFinset := hs_sub he_in_s\\n    rw [SimpleGraph.mem_edgeFinset] at he_in_edges\\n    rw [he_eq] at he_in_edges\\n    rw [SimpleGraph.mem_edgeSet] at he_in_edges\\n    have h_not_adj : ¬ G.Adj u v := hI u hu v hv\\n\n<truncated 1985 bytes>","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_1facfd37\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Updating Challenge_1facfd37.lean and checking\"","toolSummary":"\"Update and check Challenge_1facfd37.lean\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
